Inclusion criteria:
1. •	Individuals aged at least 18 years;
2. •	Pain intensity of at least 30 on a self-administered 11-point pain numeric rating scale (0: no pain to 100: maximal pain);
3. •	Pain involving the base of the thumb;
4. •	X-ray evidence of trapezometacarpial osteoarthritis with at least two of the following items involving the trapezometacarpial joint: osteophytes, joint space narrowing, subchondral bone sclerosis, or subchondral cysts;
5. •	1990 ACR classification criteria for hand osteoarthritis adapted to trapezometacarpial osteoarthritis.
6. •	Affiliation with a mode of social security (profit or being entitled).
7. •	Negative pregnancy test in women of childbearing potential
Exclusion criteria:
1. •	Secondary osteoarthritis;
2. •	Use of IM, IV or oral corticosteroids for up to 2 months.
3. •	Protected adults (including individual under guardianship by court order)
4. •	Pregnant women and lactation; lack of contraception for women of childbearing potential
5. •	Patient participating in another investigational therapeutic study
6. •	Patient unable to speak and read French
7. •	History of thumb surgery, inflammatory or crystal-associated rheumatic disease, or epilepsy;
8. •	Contra-indication to onabotulinumtoxinA;
9. •	Neurological disorders involving the hands other than carpal tunnel syndrome;
10. •	Collagen disorders involving the hands
11. •	Osteoarthritis predominating at the scaphotrapezial joint on x-ray;
12. •	Bilateral trapezometacarpial osteoarthritis without a predominant painful side;
13. •	Hand or wrist trauma for up to 2 months;
14. •	Intra-articular treatments for up to 2 months;
